WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.099
And this one's a big one, okay?

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.020
Okay.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:04.800
Okay, um...

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:07.920
um...

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:10.320
Did you love me?

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.920
Hi, I'm Paulo and I'm a director here at Jubilee.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:14.740
As you all know,

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.640
we've been living in this global pandemic and

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.720
time of social isolation

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.020
and I've been sensing that people are feeling lonely

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.300
and longing for human connection.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.400
More people have been calling their families and friends, doing group calls.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:33.700
And it just made me realize that this is a perfect opportunity for people to reconnect.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:39.820
And so we wanted to make a series where we challenge people to muster up the courage, get out of their comfort zones, and

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.240
call people they might have had a falling-out with.

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:44.240
I am calling an old friend.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:46.060
Well, I'm calling my dad.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:47.480
I'm calling...

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.100
my ex-boyfriend.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.500
I'm about to call my dad.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:51.960
Some reached out,

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:54.240
reconnected and took the leap.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:01.140
When I was younger I actually moved to Alaska.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:03.280
When I got there I was a loner,

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:07.020
I was the kid that no one really talked to, I was the loser, but not Kim.

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:09.580
She definitely was the one that spoke to me.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:12.140
She accepted me for who I was.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:16.600
I want to ask her if the reason why she stopped talking to me was because

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:17.960
she had a boyfriend.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:20.100
I'm calling my dad.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:23.960
I feel like he neglected me as a daughter. There were so many lies,

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.940
there is so much mistrust.

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:30.140
I really want to connect and understand if he still sees me as his daughter or

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:33.440
if he's still willing to see me in the future.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:37.649
I guess you can say he was like my first love, you know.

00:01:37.649 --> 00:01:40.960
Like, that somebody you're always gonna have the most feelings for.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:42.820
The day that we kind of just ended it

00:01:42.820 --> 00:01:47.880
was the day he told me that he was signing another six-year contract to go to Guam.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:48.680
And he was like,

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:53.240
"I think we should just be friends." and that was like the last thing we said to each other. So...

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:56.640
I still want to express like the fact that I'm still like in love with him,

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:00.240
but it's also like we left off at like a weird spot.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:03.880
My dad has been in and out of my life.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:08.000
Around sixth grade I decided,  you know, not to have anything-

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.440
I didn't wanna have anything to do with him and you know, he reached out to me many times,

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:14.400
but I kept denying his effort.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.340
Around this time last year,

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:26.180
I was in a fatal car accident and during rehab, I was isolated most of the time so I had a *lot* of

00:02:26.180 --> 00:02:32.820
time and room for you know self-reflection and improvement and that's why I'm here today,

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:35.040
taking the leap.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:39.300
Even last night knowing that I was gonna do this, I couldn't sleep.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:44.940
I just... I... my mind is just racing. It's going a thousand miles an hour.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.200
Hyshler: Heeeey!

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.760
Kim: It's been a while!

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:57.320
Hyshler:  It's been a while, it's so good to see you.

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:00.260
Kim: It's good to see you too. You look good!

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:04.800
Hyshler:  Thank you, you know working out little bit, just a little bit, not a lot.

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:07.160
I'm just very shaky,

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:09.420
I'm very scared.

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:13.080
I just expect that he's going to give me an apology.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:20.900
Papa: Yes?

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.520
Kathylynn: Hi, Papa!

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:24.100
Papa: Hello

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:27.100
Kathylynn: What happened?

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:28.940
Papa: What do you mean "What happened"?

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.440
Kathylynn: What happened to your hair?

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:32.540
Papa: Oh, I just woke up.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:34.280
I'm not ready.

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:39.480
Julia: Hello?

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:40.780
Gil: Hey, what's up?

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:44.040
Julia: Okay, so are you ready for this?

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:46.500
Gil: Uhh... yeah, why not

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:49.220
Julia: I'm gonna be asking you some questions,

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:54.340
because I want to like, it's like a whole thing where you can like reconnect with people.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:59.020
And like, you were the person I wanted to reconnect with.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:02.760
A lot of these questions are gonna be like about our relationship.

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:07.580
So yes, get ready.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:08.920
Gil: I was born ready.

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:10.060
Julia: Yes, okay.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:12.100
I'm about to take the leap.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:14.760
Wish me luck.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:18.860
Daja: Okay, again, thank you for being here.

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:23.200
Do I have permission to record.. to record this?

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:24.380
Dad: Yes, you sure do.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:29.600
Hyshler:  When I first moved to Alaska, you were one of my first friends, and you made me feel

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:35.900
important, you made me feel loved, you made me feel welcomed and then there was this period of time.

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:41.420
Um... and still kind of current where we just don't talk

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:43.380
Kim: Yeah, there was a-

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:47.580
a sudden drop in communication from both of us.

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:51.840
Right around when I started... dating

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:57.000
Hyshler: That's actually, that's funny that you say that 'cause...

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:59.100
That's what I was gonna ask you.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:03.220
like why did that happen? Like, why did you...

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:07.120
I guess cut off.. or not cut off our friendship, but,

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:12.560
why... yeah, I guess why did you cut it off, yeah?

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:13.180
Kim: Well

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:15.900
It wasn't intentional.

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:18.300
That relationship was not healthy.

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:21.800
Hyshler: I felt like...

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.580
Maybe it was me.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:29.740
You know you got like the new shiny toy so you just like 'discard me.'

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:34.380
You know, like that's how I felt and you know, I- I just for a long time

00:05:34.380 --> 00:05:35.440
I was really bitter.

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:38.540
Kim: You know that relationship- because that relationship is done.

00:05:39.540 --> 00:05:40.040
Hyshler: Is done?

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:43.320
Kim: That's over. Yeah I got out of that

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:46.040
Hyshler: Oh my God.

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:49.480
Kim: Maybe we can text, y'know, and it can be like old times

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:50.640
Hyshler: Yes!

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:52.640
Kim: Which would be awesome,

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:54.560
Because, you know, non-stop laughter!

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:55.060
Hyshler: Yeah.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:05:58.360
Kim: You know, I miss that. I do.

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:03.280
I know that I was a healthier person when I had that in my life.

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:04.960
Hyshler: Same, same.

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:08.740
Kim: So, I'm very happy that you reached out to me.

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:13.900
Hyshler: I hope that, you know, this is like the start of something new um...

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:16.580
Shout out to High School Musical.

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:23.200
And I will talk to you later.

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:25.220
Kim: Alright, you better!

00:06:25.220 --> 00:06:26.320
Hyshler: Yes, I will.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:31.180
Kathylynn: Like I know we haven't been talking for a while.

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:34.360
I just wanted to know if you like still like...

00:06:35.409 --> 00:06:37.409
Like want to see me again?

00:06:38.379 --> 00:06:39.780
Like in person.

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:41.760
Like you haven't seen us since-

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:42.460
Papa: You said ' I want to see you' right?

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:47.160
Yeah, you haven't seen us in a while. Like you haven't seen me since I was in middle school.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:50.920
Papa: Okay, so do you want me to visit you or you want to visit me?

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:55.600
Kathylynn: I-I mean, how come you haven't visited us?

00:06:57.080 --> 00:06:57.960
Papa: I can't,

00:06:58.160 --> 00:06:59.300
Kathylynn: Why?

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:00.940
Papa: I don't know where you live.

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:02.940
Kathylynn: You never asked!

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:05.880
Papa: No, [I've] always asked your mom.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:10.480
Kathylynn: You're the one who told me face to face that I am no longer your daughter.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:13.110
And you tell that to Caitlyn too and I don't

00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:16.739
understand why you would say that, and at the same time tell me that you still love me.

00:07:17.350 --> 00:07:19.260
Like why would you say that you love me?

00:07:19.260 --> 00:07:23.010
If you don't try to come see us and deny it right in front of the court.

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:25.010
Papa: Okay, what I did-

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:29.520
What I said to you before, 'I don't like you guys anymore'

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:31.520
But what you did to me.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:33.800
You know, first

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:37.860
I have a big problem [with] you, what you did to me.

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:40.780
Kathylynn: What did I do? What did I do to you?

00:07:40.780 --> 00:07:43.460
Papa: Okay, you did not respect me

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:45.980
Kathylynn: Have you thought about how you respected us?

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:50.220
Have you thought about how many lies you said about my mom?

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:52.590
Have you thought of that? Where's the respect in that?

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:54.580
How come you can't respect your own daughters?

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:59.040
Papa: Okay just- just stop this conversation, okay?

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:02.020
It's not gonna happen for that thing, okay?

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:04.160
We're not going to solve this problem, okay?

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:07.780
You're getting old soon, okay?

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:11.320
Just realize what your mom did to me.

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:12.820
Kathylynn: Okay, alright.

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:16.060
Okay, Papa, I'll catch you later.

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:17.700
Papa: Okay.

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:18.800
Kathylynn: Okay, bye.

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:30.720
Julia: Okay.

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:31.740
Umm...

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:38.820
Do you believe like the question "right person - wrong time"?

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:42.240
Gil: Yeah,

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:46.020
Definitely in a heartbeat, I would go back to it if I could,

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:48.440
But it wouldn't be the best decision

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:50.980
Or the healthiest decision, for either of us.

00:08:51.200 --> 00:08:51.700
Julia: Yeah.

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:55.820
Gil: You want to up to school in New York and

00:08:56.420 --> 00:08:58.420
I'm going to a different country.

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:03.440
Julia: This one's a big one, okay?

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:05.440
Okay, um..

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:08.040
um...

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:10.120
Did you love me?

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:12.020
Gil: Yes!

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:16.260
Julia: Okay.

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:18.260
Gil: I did.

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:24.000
Julia: I was thinking- like I was thinking about it and I remember it like.. the first time you said it your way.

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:27.580
And um... you called me,

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:29.900
and you were like...

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:33.460
Ooh, gosh, you were like, "I have something to tell you."

00:09:33.460 --> 00:09:36.060
He was like "I hope you're sitting down right now."

00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:37.660
Do you remember?

00:09:37.660 --> 00:09:38.220
Gil: Yeah.

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:42.200
Julia: And you were like, "I'm about to knock your socks off," and I was like,

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:46.140
"Why? Like what are you gonna say to me right now?"

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:47.120
And you were like,

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:50.040
"I love you." And I was like "What?!"

00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:52.880
Gil: Yeah.

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:56.060
Julia: Was it hard to end the relationship?

00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:58.920
Gil: Was it hard to end it?

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:00.820
Gil: Yeah.

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.200
I still think about it a lot.

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:08.780
Gill: Alright.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:09.700
Julia: Thank you.

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:12.500
Gil: You're very welcome, I'll be around tonight if you need me.

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:13.560
Julia: Okay, bye.

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:16.620
Oh my God...

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:21.820
Daja: Okay.

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:24.680
Again, thank you for being here.

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:30.200
The last time we met there were like 11-12 years of resentment and..

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:33.760
you know things that were unsaid?

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:38.560
Well, I was brutally honest and at the same time, I wasn't truthful...

00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:40.540
and I was having trouble, you know,

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:47.980
facing the things that I can and can't change and one of those things is that... you are my dad.

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:53.380
Dad: You know, I had the same problems, like with my dad as well

00:10:53.380 --> 00:10:58.040
And trying to learn how to love him and forgive him for not being a part of my life.

00:10:58.040 --> 00:11:01.760
So I get it, and you're a lot like me.

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:06.260
I have a hard time verbalizing and saying how I honestly feel.

00:11:06.260 --> 00:11:08.260
So, yeah, I get it.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:13.040
Daja: I did this, came on here just to tell you that...

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:14.500
That I...

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:20.700
That I forgive you,

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:25.580
that I chose- and I choose you. And if you ever wondered...

00:11:26.280 --> 00:11:29.220
that if I ever loved you... that-

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:33.180
that I forgive you... so..-

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:37.520
Dad: I appreciate you forgiving me, that means the world to me, to hear you say that.

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:38.580
Wow...

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:40.680
That was huge for you, huh?

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:42.440
Daja: Yeah. Yeah.

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:44.960
Dad: Are we going to meet once a month?

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:47.360
You know, you come here or I come there or

00:11:47.360 --> 00:11:49.360
Are we going to talk or text frequently?

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:50.680
like, I don't know

00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:53.120
I kind of need an after action plan.

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:55.120
Daja: Seeing each other once a month sounds...

00:11:57.280 --> 00:11:59.580
Really good.

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:02.160
Again, thank you, thank you, thank you.

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:03.240
Dad: You're welcome, love you

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:05.720
Daja: I'm gonna end it now.

00:12:06.040 --> 00:12:09.380
This... this was a lot for me in that moment.

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:11.780
In that moment, it was, you know, just a lot.

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:16.360
And now I'm just, you know, just letting-

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:17.920
just letting it go and...

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:20.300
I feel... lighter.

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:23.120
Which you know, I'm a heavy individual,

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:25.440
but I feel lighter.

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:27.120
He didn't answer my questions at all.

00:12:27.980 --> 00:12:29.980
I'm just going to be happy for him.

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:32.980
That's... that's just it. I'm happy for him...

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:35.420
after everything.

00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:38.060
I look like a mess.

00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:44.040
There is so much closure... and I honestly...

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:46.570
If...

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:51.600
you need to call someone right now and tell them, "Hey,

00:12:52.260 --> 00:12:54.700
I love you. Hey, I miss you.",

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:58.560
take this as an opportunity.

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:01.400
You never know unless you try.

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:03.840
I hope you enjoyed that episode.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:08.820
I just want to say thank you to all the people who submitted videos, were brave and

00:13:08.820 --> 00:13:11.520
willing to be vulnerable on camera.

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:13.300
Thank you so much.

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:16.820
And... if you're interested in maybe reaching out or reconnecting with

00:13:16.820 --> 00:13:18.600
someone and taking the leap,

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:20.780
then click on the link in the description below

00:13:20.780 --> 00:13:23.280
and maybe you can be featured in a future episode.

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:26.480
Thanks for watching and until next time.

